; claude: what a page's elements look like (see web/README.md,
; plan_browser_teaching.md): Looks, Mosaic's fixed table computed down
; the tree; and the page's style sheets cascaded on top of it: Css_syntax
; (the text read: tokens, blocks, rules), Selectors (which elements a
; rule is for), Css (the cascade); and TinyChrome's (plan_tiny_chrome.md):
; Css_values (lengths, colours, calc(), var()), Cascade (@media, origins,
; the rule index), Computed (a style per element, over ua.css: Ua_sheet). Pure OCaml, no shapes: a
; look is numbers and flags, the app draws it.
(library
 (name web_style)
 (package elm_playground)
 (wrapped false)
 (libraries web_html) ; Dom
)

; claude: the browser's own style sheet, ua.css, embedded as a string
(rule
 (targets Ua_sheet.ml)
 (deps ua.css)
 (action
  (with-stdout-to
   %{targets}
   (progn
    (echo "(* generated from ua.css by libs/web/style/dune *)\n")
    (echo "let text = {|")
    (cat ua.css)
    (echo "|}\n")))))
